[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Nothing to Worry About]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.32]Lesson 39 | 第39课
[00:02.19]Nothing to worry about | 不必担心
[00:10.93]What was the differnce between Bruce's behaviour and that of other people? | 布鲁斯的行为与其他人有什么不同？
[00:18.55]The rough road across the plain soon became so bad that we tried to get Bruce to drive back to the village we had come from. | 穿越平原的崎岖道路很快变得非常糟糕，我们试图劝说布鲁斯调头，返回我们出发来的那个村庄。
[00:28.49]Even though the road was littered with boulders and pitted with holes, Bruce was not in the least perturbed. | 尽管道路遍布巨石、坑坑洼洼，但布鲁斯一点也不慌张。
[00:37.64]Glancing at his map, he informed us that the next village was a mere twenty miles away. | 他瞥了一眼地图，告诉我们下一个村庄离这儿仅20英里。
[00:45.62]It was not that Bruce always underestimated difficulties. | 这并不是说布鲁斯总是低估困难，
[00:49.76]He simply had no sense of danger at all. | 而是他根本就没有危险的概念。
[00:53.87]No matter what the conditions were, he believed that a car should be driven as fast as it could possibly go. | 无论路况如何，他都认为应该把车开到最快。
[01:02.58]As we bumped over the dusty track, we swerved to avoid large boulders. | 我们在尘土飞扬的路面上颠簸前行，急转弯绕开大巨石。
[01:08.47]The wheels scooped up stones which hammered ominously under the car. | 车轮卷起的石块在车身下敲击作响，听着不吉利。
[01:14.90]We felt sure that sooner or later a stone would rip a hole in our petrol tank or damage the engine. | 我们确信，一块石头迟早会把油箱砸个洞或者损坏发动机。
[01:23.60]Because of this, we kept looking back, wondering if we were leaving a trail of oil and petrol behind us. | 因此，我们不断回头看，怀疑身后是否留下了一道油迹和汽油痕迹。
[01:33.22]What a relief it was when the boulders suddenly disappeared, | 巨石突然消失时，我们真是如释重负，
[01:37.45]giving way to a stretch of plain where the only obstacles were clumps bushes. | 眼前出现了一片平原，唯一的障碍只是一簇簇灌木丛。
[01:44.64]But there was worse to come. Just ahead of us there was a huge fissure. | 但更糟的还在后面。就在我们前方，有一道巨大的裂缝。
[01:51.80]In response to renewed pleadings, Bruce stopped. | 在我们一再恳求之下，布鲁斯停了车。
[01:56.77]Though we all got out to examine the fissure, he remained in the car. | 我们都下车查看那道裂缝，他却待在车里。
[02:02.09]We informed him that the fissure extended for fifty yards and was two feet wide and four feet deep. | 我们告诉他，裂缝长50码、宽2英尺、深4英尺。
[02:11.31]Even this had no effect. | 即使这也无济于事。
[02:14.88]Bruce went into a low gear and drove at a terrifying speed, | 布鲁斯挂上低速挡，以惊人的速度向裂缝冲去，
[02:20.67]keeping the front wheels astride the crack as he followed its zigzag course. | 让前轮分跨在裂缝两侧，沿着之字形的裂缝走向前进。
[02:27.14]Before we had time to worry about what might happen, we were back on the plain again. | 我们还没来得及担心会发生什么，就又回到了平原上。
[02:34.67]Bruce consulted the map once more and told us that the village was now only fifteen miles away. | 布鲁斯再次查看地图，告诉我们那个村庄现在只有15英里了。
[02:43.24]Our next obstacle was a shallow pool of water about half a mile across. | 下一个障碍是一片宽约半英里的浅水塘。
[02:49.12]Bruce charged at it, but in the middle, the car came to a grinding halt. | 布鲁斯向水塘冲去，但到了中间，车子“嘎吱”一声停住了。
[02:55.96]A yellow light on the dashboard flashed angrily and Bruce cheerfully announced that there was no oil in the engine! | 仪表盘上一盏黄灯怒气冲冲地闪烁，布鲁斯兴高采烈地宣布发动机里没有油了！
